In article <TALVOLA.90Jan21094710@janus.berkeley.edu> talvola@janus.berkeley.edu (Erik Talvola) writes:
     I was running Nethack 3.0 PL6 (the binary from lampwick) and I noticed
   a bug in the way help files worked.  On the first level, I went into
   the help and could access all the different help files.  However, after
   I went down a couple of levels, I couldn't get the first 3 or so help
   screens.  I would try to get the list of commands, and it just returned
   me to the game without printing anything.  Has anyone seen this behavior?


I have the same version of NetHack (3.0 pl 6) and I have seen that behavior
quite often. It happens randomly, I don't know why. I tried to remove it
by increasing FILES= in CONFIG.SYS from 20 to 25, but it did'n help.
There's another bug, too. Sometimes it says 'Bad command or file name'
when the game is about to end (when I die or save, or possibly win...).
Sometimes it hangs the whole system, but usually not. The game itself is
quite stable, I have only once got the message 'Program in disorder, perhaps
you'd better quit'.


